# Responsive first

Design admin pages for every viewport. Do not ship a desktop-only layout and patch phones later.

- Mobile-first breakpoints: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`.
- Stack on small screens; add columns only when space allows.
- Keep tap targets usable. Avoid horizontal scroll unless the content needs it (wide tables use a clear overflow).
- Check ~375px, ~768px, and ~1280px before finishing UI work.
- Prefer `%`, `fr`, and `minmax` over fixed pixel widths for page chrome.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="grid grid-cols-4 gap-4">...</div>
<aside className="w-[320px]">...</aside>

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">...</div>
<aside className="w-full md:w-64 lg:w-80">...</aside>
```

Stay with patterns already in `admin/` (evergreen browsers). Do not add bleeding-edge CSS that the app does not already use.
